Those are really elaborate.  I just test for non-cursedness; drop the
single piece and stand next to it, wait 20 or so turns to see if my
pet walks on it.  I'll wait longer if it's a really cool piece (e.g. I
find mithril before the mines, or for magic boots/gloves/etc).  It
REALLY helps to have a tripe ration in your inventory, since your pet
will stay near you and it's pretty obvious if he's avoiding the item
or not.

I do this basically immediately with all armor that's got a base as
good as what I'm wearing, and with all rings/amulets and my first
pick-axe.  For instance, if I'm wearing an orcish helm I'll keep
testing all the orcish helms I find and putting them on if they're ok,
until I either get a dwarvish helm or find a +1 orcish helm.  Of
course, with potential magic stuff (cloaks, crested/visored/etc helms,
boots, gloves, etc) I'll test anything I haven't identified.

