SPOILER:












Learn to price-identify scrolls.  Identify is about 30 Zorkmids,
Enchant weapon is about 80, Enchant Armor and Remove Curse are about
100.  Prices affected by Charisma, whether you're a Tourist, and
whether you wear a dunce cap or Hawaiian Shirt (shirt has to be
visible--armor over it eliminates the effect)

And obviously ditto for lamps.  The one that's over 30 Zorkmids is
magic (usually 60-80ish I think), the cheap one is mundane.  If you
find either one, #name it--if the lighting shop only has a mundane
one, #name it that and then you'll know that when you find an un#named
lamp that you should bless it and #rub it.

For a while I was #name'ing everything in every shop I came to with
its price, but it turns out just labelling those scrolls and lamps is
enough and much less of a pain.  The other scrolls are tough to
distinguish (might be worth it once you've identified enough), as are
rings/potions/wands (though making a note of really pricey ones will
help you find that rare early /ofDeathorWishing and mark it for
immediate identification)

